WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.599
To many young Americans, suburbs are
boring, economically stagnant, socially

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:13.769
monolithic places filled with
Republicans. But data from AEI's Survey on

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:18.240
Community and Society shows that suburbs
are actually politically diverse places

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.170
where younger Americans have vibrant
social lives and dynamic economic

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:27.449
opportunities. 21% of suburbanites are
liberal, and 16% are conservative. Most

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:32.240
suburbanites fall in the middle of the
ideological spectrum. 85% of 18- to

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.000
29-year-olds who live in the suburbs say that
they are living in a good or excellent

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.100
place. In contrast, only 70% of younger
urbanites rate their cities as good or

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.390
excellent places to live. Young suburbanites are also more likely to

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.379
regularly talk to their neighbors,
compared to those in cities. And when it

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:53.340
comes to the economy, the attitudes of
younger Americans toward their finances

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.809
and career are as bullish in the suburbs
as they are in the cities. The data is

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:01.920
clear: Younger Americans thrive socially
and economically in suburbs, which offer

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.320
space, safety, convenience and political
diversity.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.460
Would you like to live in an

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:12.680
urban, suburban, or rural area? Let us know
in our poll. Also, let us know what other

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:17.280
topics you'd like our scholars to cover
in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.159
subscribe for more research and videos
from AEI.

